SINGLE RESPONSIBILITY PRINCIPLE (SRP)

Definition:
A class should have ONLY ONE reason to change.

In simple words:
👉 One class = One job

------------------------------------

WHY SRP IS IMPORTANT?

1. Easier to maintain
   - Changes are localized
   - Less risk of breaking other logic

2. Better readability
   - Easy to understand what a class does

3. Easier testing
   - Each responsibility can be tested independently

4. Better scalability
   - You can extend features without modifying existing logic

------------------------------------

SRP IN ANDROID CONTEXT

❌ Bad:
Activity / Fragment doing:
- API calls
- Database access
- UI logic
- Business rules

✅ Good:
- Repository → API / Data source
- Database class → Persistence
- View / Compose → UI
- ViewModel → Business logic

------------------------------------

INTERVIEW ONE-LINER

"SRP means a class should focus on only one responsibility.
If a class has multiple reasons to change, it violates SRP."

------------------------------------

REAL ANDROID EXAMPLE

Activity / Compose:
- Displays UI

ViewModel:
- Handles logic

Repository:
- Fetches data

Database:
- Stores data

Each layer has ONE job → SRP followed ✔
